    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b2f9afef-2213-5cf4-8ac2-9379af1651a3",
      ":question/problem": "Use the substitution $u=x^{3}$. Which integral is obtained?\n\n$$\n\\int x^{2} \\csc^{2}{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=x^{3}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=3 x^{2}.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int x^{2} \\csc^{2}{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed integral is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
